<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21341] sanityn test_51b: file size is 1024, should be 3145728</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21341</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7d5f0105-9a3a-43df-bfca-cde357ed117a" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7d5f0105-9a3a-43df-bfca-cde357ed117a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_51b failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;file size is 1024, should be 3145728
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.66&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137763" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137763&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.66&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137763" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137763&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanityn test_51b fails intermittently with "file size is 1024, should be 3145728": the stat on $DIR2 is delayed by fail_loc 0x1404 (glimpse delay) but returns the stale size 1024. In the failing run the delayed glimpse (cfs_fail_timeout id 1404, 4000ms) fired twice (once per dd and stat) and the dd took 4.07s, so the test's 0.2s sleep ordering did not hold under the slow ZFS VMs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a timing race in the test, not a patch regression. Same error on other changes and branch runs in the last 30 days: master-next full-zfs-part-3 2026-11-20 (session ceba04ac-9daa-4acc-b600-bc40b74671f9), change 69694 ps5 review-dne-zfs-part-5 2026-11-01, change 69966 ps3 review-dne-zfs-part-5 2026-10-29. Rate about 0.1 to 0.2 percent of runs; 68 failures with this error since 2024-12.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13753" title="sanityn test_51b: 'file size is 1024, should be 3145728' " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13753"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13753&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (Resolved/Fixed in 2020, test timeout increase landed 2020-08-27) tracks the same error and has had +1s on master through 2026-08-05, so its fix did not hold. Raised new, linked Related to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13753" title="sanityn test_51b: 'file size is 1024, should be 3145728' " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13753"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13753&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/68620" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68620&lt;/a&gt; patchset 23 (session 78a639db-b2be-4530-92b5-3e8ba4c3d285, review-dne-zfs-part-2, el10.2 zfs), where the series changes only the DIO and buffered folio paths.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-68620-ps24-0b2c42d45fe4 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/68620" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68620&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
